### 3.8 Raw spectra of \(K^{0}_{s}\) and \(\Lambda\)+\(\overline{\Lambda}\)

The raw yield can be calculated by integrating the Gaussian fit function. However, this method always under-estimates the signal under the mass peak, we use direct bin counting for the raw yield estimation. We sum the counts over all the mass bins within a mass window, \(\pm 3\sim 4\sigma\) away from the center of the peak, then subtract the counts under the background fit line within the same mass window. Finally, the summed counts are normalized to the number of events in a specific centrality.

